<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis Garnier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a>–<a href="/years/1873">1873</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Marie Joseph François Garnier</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis Garnier was a French naval officer and explorer. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> exploration expedition of 1866–1868 after the death of its commander, Ernest Doudart de Lagrée, showing that the river was not a navigable route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Sent to Tonkin in 1873, he seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> citadel without authorisation and was killed in December 1873 in an ambush by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-flag-army">Black Flag Army</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-garnier.jpg" alt="Francis Garnier" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Sarrut (1822-????) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lieutenant_Francis_Garnier_in_the_early_1870s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
